
1. Characteristics of immunity system in postoperative delirium patients by single-cell transcriptomic analysis
(Submitter supplied) Background: Postoperative delirium (POD) is the most complication after cardiac surgery, and associated with increased mortality and decreased long term cognition ability. Our study aimed to explore the characteristics of immunity system in POD patients. Methods: This prospective study included patients scheduled for selective on-pump cardiac surgeries, who were divided into Non-POD and POD group according to whether POD occurred within 30 days after surgery. more...
